    {
      "id": "jzs0wfb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction to Branches of Biology"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Biological science is divided into foundational branches including Genetics, Botany, Zoology, and Microbiology.",
        "Modern biological applications expand into specialized domains such as Biotechnology and Ecology.",
        "Comprehensive sub-branches and comparative frameworks provide a structured understanding of living organisms."
      ],
      "id": "8dwwco2"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Chapter Number",
          "value": "18",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Main Sections",
          "value": "12",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Core Fields",
          "value": "Botany & Zoology",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Applied Fields",
          "value": "Biotechnology",
          "icon": "info"
        }
      ],
      "id": "u5c7nv9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d7613ad",
      "content": "Biology is divided into several branches for systematic study of living organisms. Each branch focuses on specific aspects such as plants, animals, genes, microorganisms, environment and applied sciences."
    },
    {
      "id": "9d18d6g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Genetics"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bshpya2",
      "content": "Genetics is the branch of biology that deals with heredity and variation. It studies genes, DNA, chromosomes and inheritance patterns."
    },
    {
      "id": "p70exj1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Botany"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "755cn8u",
      "content": "Botany is the study of plants including their structure, classification, physiology and economic importance."
    },
    {
      "id": "fdw40vp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Zoology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xff1eq3",
      "content": "Zoology deals with the study of animals including their anatomy, physiology, classification and behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "owlp10u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Microbiology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eisq8h8",
      "content": "Microbiology is the study of microscopic organisms such as bacteria, viruses, fungi and protozoa."
    },
    {
      "id": "20qvi5q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Biotechnology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3btmuix",
      "content": "Biotechnology involves the use of living organisms or biological systems to develop useful products like vaccines, GM crops and medicines."
    },
    {
      "id": "bxdwpfl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Ecology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mz2pqg7",
      "content": "Ecology studies the relationship between organisms and their environment."
    },
    {
